  "scope_notes": [
    "Full matrix includes regular bounded scale cases; the previous actual million-message and over-2-GiB runs remain historical evidence, not rerun claims.",
    "MFLD2 open audits all field pages and verifies the source hash. Bounded page retention does not imply zero-scan cold start. Summaries require a trusted producer.",
    "CDR/ROS1 views avoid JSON expansion but still read/decompress enclosing Chunks. Variable arrays require a wire scan. Exact conditions over opaque binary fields fail explicitly.",
    "Protobuf selection skips unrequested top-level materialization; selected nested messages and canonical ProtoJSON retain the documented complete-decoding paths. JSON is parsed before projection.",
    "Projected payload decoding runs on the main thread while worker Chunk expansion remains available. MIDX2 worker reservations use the actual Chunk response bound.",
    "Temporal joins require ascending input, use stable first duplicate/right earlier equidistance ties, bound their own retained payloads, and stop without draining unused right tails.",
    "Recording recovery verifies all committed files, quarantines incomplete reserved tails, adopts validated complete orphans, and creates only new segment numbers. Tests cover process termination and publication windows, not power-loss durability.",
    "Core live recording requires resending uncommitted tail messages. The CLI binds a fixed source SHA256 and replays its physical committed prefix to avoid duplicates.",
    "Public ROS1 array comparisons verify scalar/inline data and large-array element/byte counts; binary export content equivalence is separately tested on independent synthetic payloads.",
